e>SAKAGUCHI MIKIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAO CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIYAJI, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKI, KAZUO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OTSUKA, KAZUHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAKAGUCHI, MIKIO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MIYAJI TAKASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OKI KAZUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OTSUKA KAZUHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SAKAGUCHI MIKIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIYAJI, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKI, KAZUO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OTSUKA, KAZUHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SAKAGUCHI, MIKIO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A composite powder which comprises (A) alkali metal silicate particles having a composition which in its anhydrous state is represented by the formula (I): xM2O.ySiO2.zMeO (wherein M represents Na and/or K; Me represents Ca and/or Mg; 0.5&lt;/=y/x&lt;/=4.0; 0&lt;/=z/x&lt;/=1.0; and the ratio of Mg/Ca in MeO is 0 to 10) and having an average particle diameter of 1 to 500  mu m and (B) water-soluble salt particles having a solubility in water at 20  DEG C of 1 g/100 g or higher and an average particle diameter of 0.01 to 50  mu m, the (A)/(B) weight ratio being from 1/9 to 99/1; and a detergent composition comprising the composite powder. In the powder, the alkali metal silicate has significantly heightened storage stability while retaining its intact ion exchange ability.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une poudre composite, comprenant (A) des particules de silicate de métal alcalin dont la composition, à l'état anhydre, est représentée par la formule (I): xM2O.ySiO2.zMeO, (dans cette formule, M représentant Na et/ou K; Me représentant Ca et/ou Mg; 0,5&lt;/=y/x&lt;/=4,0; 0&lt;/=z/x&lt;/=1,0; et le rapport entre Mg/Ca et MeO étant de 0 à 10), lesdites particules possédant un diamètre particulaire moyen de 1 à 500  mu m; et (B) des particules de sel solubles dans l'eau dont la solubilité dans l'eau à 20  DEG C est égale ou supérieure à 1g/100g, et le diamètre particulaire moyen est de 0,10 à 50  mu m; le rapport pondéral (A)/(B) étant de 1/9 à 99/1. L'invention concerne également une composition détergeante comprenant la poudre composite. Dans cette poudre, le silicate de métal alcalin possède une stabilité de stockage relativement élevée, tout en conservant intacte son aptitude à échanger des ions.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www